<title>SINGAPORE: GP Batteries full year net up 14.5 pct.</title>
<headline>GP Batteries full year net up 14.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	     23.69	vs	20.68</p>
<p>    Dividend (cts)	  8.20	vs	 7.60</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)    29.36	vs	25.96</p>
<p>    Turnover		357.68	vs     309.47</p>
<p>    Other income	    3.52	vs	 2.62</p>
<p>    Interest expense	7.48	vs	 7.49</p>
<p>    Depreciation	   17.41	vs	14.85</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	 23.82	vs	20.91</p>
<p>    Associates		2.01	vs	 1.42</p>
<p>    Tax			 1.79	vs	 1.47</p>
<p>    Minorities     (loss) 0.35	vs	 0.18 (loss)</p>
<p>Note - Maker and distributor of batteries and related products, GP Batteries International Ltd, said it achieved record turnover and profit despite keen competition from Japanese competitors due to the weakening yen. It said its regional markets performed strongly and production was expanded to meet unexpected demand for micro batteries for new electronic toys. -- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
